  "body": "### Description\r\n\r\nAll cross server contacts, do not receive my messages anymore, nor am I receiving messages from them.\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\nI guess let the SSL certificate expire and then renew it manually?\r\n\r\n### Homeserver\r\n\r\nmartinrouterking.com\r\n\r\n### Synapse Version\r\n\r\n1.67.0\r\n\r\n### Installation Method\r\n\r\npip (from PyPI)\r\n\r\n### Platform\r\n\r\nRocky Linux 9.0\r\n\r\n### Relevant log output\r\n\r\n```shell\r\nI dont see any error, that I would associate with this (to the best of my knowledge). The only warning in the logs I see is:\r\n\r\n\r\n│2022-09-15 13:42:10,181 - synapse.http.server - 743 - WARNING - GET-182 - Not sending response to request <XForwardedForRequest at 0x7f93940a3550 method='GET' uri='/_matrix/client/r0/sync?filter=0&timeout=30000&since=s18000_3485│34_12_18712_18279_6_895_13448_0' clientproto='HTTP/1.0' site='8008'>, already disconnected.   \r\n```\r\n\r\nIn the client I see one request failing with 504 (no response text) in the debug console:\r\n```\r\nhttps://martinrouterking.com/_matrix/client/r0/sync?filter=1&timeout=30000&since=s18000_348534_12_18712_18279_6_895_13448_0\r\n```\r\n```\r\n\r\n\r\n### Anything else that would be useful to know?\r\n\r\nOne thing has changed, compared to before: Now I use stackpaths ssl certificate, so the A entry of the domain goes to their server and they serve via CDN, that may be related to the problem",
